\par\par \b \uc2 Dollars trade at 4300-4500 Lebanese pounds after pledge of market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2020\par 15:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BEIRUT, June 15 (Reuters) - Scarce dollars traded at 4300-4500 Lebanese pounds on Monday, market participants said, not far from rates seen last week when the president said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's President \uc2 Michel Aoun\uc2  said on Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would start injecting dollars into the market on Monday, trying to stop a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crash that has led to economic hardship and sparked unrest.\par \par \uc2 There was no statement from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the presidency on the supply of dollars on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Market participants said there was chaos with differing exchange rates across the informal market, now a main source of cash for most people after banks imposed tight controls.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost more than 60% of its value since late last year, when Lebanon plunged deep into a financial crisis that has pushed the government to seek help from the \uc2 IMF\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The heavily indebted state has kept an official dollar peg of 1,507.5 pounds but with foreign reserves dwindling, that rate is now only available for imports of fuel, medicine, and wheat.\par \par \uc2 One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said the price of dollars was 4,300 pounds on Monday, while another dealer and a customer said the greenback changed hands at 4,500.\par \par \uc2 A second customer said he sold dollars at 4,000 pounds.\par \par \uc2 The rate had jumped to about 5,000 last week, igniting protests in several cities, but then fell to 4,500 at some exchange bureaus on Friday after Aoun's announcement.\par \par \uc2 In a bid to rein in the parallel market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a unified pricing system this month with the goal of lowering the price to 3,200. But importers have said dollars at the lower rate, which was set at 3,910 on Monday, have been unavailable. (Reporting by Ellen Francis and Tom Perry; Editing by Kirsten Donovan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-6-15T14:50:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200615eg6f02j1t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
