\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Lebanon's PM vows to curb devaluation and inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Lebanese Prime Minister Hasan Diab on Thursday pledged to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's devaluation and subsidize commodities against inflation on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Since September 2019 Lebanon has experienced the worst crisis since the end of the civil war (1975-1990), amplified by strengthening measures related to coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 The Lebanese pound lost more than half its value against the dollar, leading to inflation predictions of more than 50% in 2020.\par \par \uc2 In April, the oeneg\u233\'00\'E9 \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2  warned that more than half of the population could be unable to meet their basic needs.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor promised me that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BDL) will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market from today to protect the Lebanese pound and curb the exchange rate increase," Diab announced in a speech, coinciding with the first hundred days of his government after gaining the trust of parliament.\par \par \uc2 "I also announce that the importation of basic food products will be subsidized (...) and that Lebanese will soon see a fall in the prices of these products," he added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which since 1997 has a fixed parity against the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of 1,507 pounds per dollar on the official market, sank in recent months on the parallel market to fall below the historical threshold of 4,000 pounds per dollar.\par \par \uc2 ah/bek/mdz/pc/mb\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200521eg5l00