\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Iran's Noxious Influence on  \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon \highlight\uc2  and Iraq Crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 869 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Lebanese security forces are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to separate protesters protesting in the capital's central district of Beirut during the 13th day of anti-government protests on October 29, 2019. - An unprecedented intersectonal movement has paralyzed Lebanon's major cities since 17 October, as protesters continue to demand complete reform of the political system. (Photo by ANWAR AMRO / AFP) (AFP/)Each day that passes it is easier to observe and recognize the extent to which the Iranian regime has become unpopular in Iraq and Lebanon. This situation has nothing to do with the media coverage of Al-Arabiya TV or the hashtags of an electronic army, as Iranian regime officials claim. Across Iraq, there is no internet or social media. Iraq's government has blocked the Internet to please the Khomeinist regime, while in Tehran they reaffirm that waves of incitement come from cyberspace. However, the uprising is still alive and continues in both Iraq and Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 Tehran claims Saudi Arabia and Israel have influenced the millions of protesters who have flooded the streets of Iraqi and Lebanese cities in the past two weeks. Iran wants to close its ears to the protesters as it has been largely responsible for causing its poverty through the domination of the Shiite Khomeinist militias in bothcountries, all of which led to the failure of both governments in both Beirut and Baghdad. Reality and current chaos indicate that all accusations against the Iranian regime match reality.\par \par \uc2 All armed militias in Iraq are affiliated with Iran or its allies. In Lebanon, \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  is stronger than the Lebanese national army, and the Shiite organization is The Occupying Army of Iran in the country, so most governments around the world have been forced to refrain from dealing with Iraq and Lebanon because of the influence of and Iran in both states.\par \par \uc2 An anti-government protester waves a Lebanese flag during a protest in Beirut, Lebanon, on October 25, 2019. (AP Photo/Hassan Ammar) (Hassan Ammar/)Saudi Arabia supported Lebanon's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by depositing funds with its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while Iran caused an absolute and total depreciation due to \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 's dominance of state institutions. Lebanese is being subject to harsh financial sanctions for its economy for direct responsibility for Iran and \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 . These are well-known facts and people don't need TV channels or hashtags to know the source of their economic misery and the monster that's closing their rights and freedoms.\par \par \uc2 In Iraq, the Iranian project was based on the seizure and hijacking of state institutions: Parliament, political parties and the armed forces were seenforced to incorporate Iran's militias into their soil. Thus, the situation worsened and people rose up in Iraq, not as Sunnis against Shiites, nor as a party against another. The uprising was not led by the remnants of \uc2 Saddam Hussein\uc2 's Baath Party, nor did the black flag of ISIS criminal extremism be raised. The Iraqi uprising is purely peaceful and patriotic, despite attempts by the Iranian media to describe it as driven by the United States and Israel. Their spectrum is broad and their demands refute their accusations.Peaceful protests have taken place in Baghdad, Basra, Karbala, Nayaf and other parts of Iraq, almost all of these governorates have a Shia majority posing lawsuits that all support. They demand an end to corruption, an improvement in government performance, and the elimination of armed terrorist militias under Iran's influence.\par \par \uc2 Protesters call for Iraq's independence and respect for its Arab identity. While Iran threatens to demolish everything over the heads of 30 million Iraqis if they stand in their Persian-Islamic expansionist project of governing and controlling the country.\par \par \uc2 In Lebanon, the movement has similar characteristics. Protests are against government corruption, mafias and sctorysm. Mass protests took place not only in Beirut, but also in large cities such as Tripoli (mostly Sunni) and Nabatieh and Baalbek (mostly Shiites).\par \par \uc2 Anti-government demonstrators shout slogans and wave flags in downtown Beirut on Sunday, October 20, 2019. (AP Photo/Hussein Mesh) (Hussein Mesh/)Christian protesters have called for the elimination of corrupt Christian ministers, so were Sunnis the first to demand the resignation of Prime Minister \uc2 Saad Hariri\uc2  (Sunni), and many Shiite clerics expressed their rejection of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  ( completely pro-irani shiite). It has become clear that the calamitous economic situation of Lebanese citizens has tested people's patience and caused them to break their silence.\par \par \uc2 It is known that in terms of arms, the balance of power is not on the side of the protesters either in Lebanon or Iraq, but their resolve and determination, as their massive public support, will bring about significant and minimal changes, their message has already been sent to the community in ternational.\par \par \uc2 What remains to be known is "if that message of rejection of expansionist terrorism by the Iranian regime, as well as the corruption of its local politicians and the mafias in the shadows of power was received by the free world." And in such a case, that temperament will take the international community with the regional leaders of these issues.\par \par \uc2 MORE ON THIS THEME:\par \par \uc2 Lebanon: those behind the crisis\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020191102efb200432\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
