\par\par \b \uc2 Lebanon pound hovers below band on regional upset.  \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 17:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BEIRUT, March 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's pound hovered just below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in interbank trade this week as concern over Middle East tensions crept into the market, dealers said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 They said the pound was changing hands at 1,514-1,516 to the dollar in interbank trade, just outside the weakest end of the 1,501-1,514 band. Officially the band was trading at 1,514.  \par \par \uc2 "There is a bit of tense situation, political and regional," said one dealer. "But there is still no pressure on the pound. There's just not much offer on the dollar."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the tune of $7-10 million a day, but there was no rush.  \par \par \uc2 Regional tensions rose this week after Israel killed Sheikh Ahmed Yassin, founder of the militant Palestinian Hamas group, drawing widespread criticism and vows of revenge.  \par \par \uc2 Lebanese Hizbollah guerrillas retaliated with attacks on Israeli positions in a disputed border area. An Israeli air strike also killed two Palestinians trying to fire rockets into Israel from south Lebanon.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the effects of a special high-yielding CD offer, which required banks to sell dollars to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , were also lingering in the market.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped the offer, which had boosted its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, last year but some banks had bought the certificates of deposit on a forward deal.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped the CD offer in October and resumed treasury bill auctions, which it had suspended for nine months after receiving about $4 billion in soft loans from international lenders in 2002 to help ease its debt service.  \par \par \uc2 The pound strengthened after that debt aid summit but has since slipped as the government has failed to make good on long-delayed privatisations pledged to lenders at the time.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040326e03q002fs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
