\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound unshaken by Hizbollah killing. \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2003\par 15:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Aug 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's pound trod water well inside the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band this week, apparently unshaken by the killing of a Hizbollah guerrilla group member, traders said on Friday. They said the pound was trading at about 1,512-1,513 to the dollar, off the weakest end of the 1,501-1,514 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. The interbank rate was steady at about four percent. "The mood is in favour of the pound because the interest rate spread is attractive," said one trader. "The bombing did not affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all. This shows the pound is not being badly hit by politics." \par \par \uc2  A member of Lebanon's Hizbollah group was killed on Saturday by a bomb planted in his car. Hizbollah blamed Israel and vowed revenge. \par \par \uc2  The Syrian and Iranian-backed group attacked Israeli troops in a disputed border area on Friday, drawing Israel air raids on Lebanese border villages. The Lebanese pound has been affected by domestic political spats and regional upheaval in the past, but traders said the market had largely discounted such risks. \par \par \uc2  Lebanon's pound had come under severe pressure over the past two years as fears mounted over the government's ability to service the roughly $30 billion public debt, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The pound rose after a debt aid summit late last year, which drew $4 billion in cheap loans to help Lebanon cope with the debt burden. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been further boosted in recent weeks by an influx of tourists from the oil-rich Gulf. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030808dz8800qut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
