\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanon to probe laundering charges at troubled bank. \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2003\par 15:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, July 11 (Reuters) - A Lebanese prosecutor plans to probe possible money laundering and check fraud by officials at Bank al-Madina, court sources said on Friday, in the latest step to secure deposits at the troubled bank. \par \par \uc2  Rising speculation that the small Beirut bank could not meet its commitments rattled local markets in February, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in to reassure depositors. \par \par \uc2  Recent Lebanese media reports said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had frozen accounts of some bank officials to ensure it meets outstanding obligations of more than $200 million to depositors. \par \par \uc2  The prosecutor's probe is expected to bolster government efforts to protect the bank's depositors. \par \par \uc2  Bank sector sources said on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had appointed a temporary manager for Bank al-Madina and an affiliated institution, United Credit, after its existing management failed to make good on obligations to depositors. \par \par \uc2  Representatives of the temporary administrator, contacted at the bank's offices, declined to elaborate on the status of its assets, obligations or accounts. \par \par \uc2  No immediate comment was available from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The latest developments involving Bank al-Madina did not appear to be unsettling the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, although they raised the prospect of instability in the country's financial sector - long a haven for Arab investors and an affluent Lebanese diaspora due to its tradition of banking secrecy. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has periodically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the the administration of troubled banks, injected capital into them or provided soft loans to encourage their acquisition by stronger banks in order to keep the sector stable. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030711dz7b00q34\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
