\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound steady on progress in mobile sector. \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2002\par 13:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Aug 9 (Reuters) - The Lebanese pound remained firm in the week ending Friday as traders said progress towards an agreement with cellular phone operators aimed at privatisation of the sector improved sentiment in the market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the pound was trading around 1,512-1,513 pounds to the dollar on the interbank market, well within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 1,501-1,514. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's cabinet approved a proposal on Thursday to offer cellular phone operators Cellis and LibanCell $36-$38 million each to run the sector ahead of privatisation, key to handling a $28.8 billion public debt. \par \par \uc2  Plans for a sell-off have been slowed by government infighting. \par \par \uc2  "They are obliged to arrive at a solution for the cellular phones," said one trader, who saw the decision as one step toward resolving the government squabbling. \par \par \uc2  Mobile revenues are set to revert to the state at the end of the month as a step toward privatising the sector, which has been the site of long-running legal battles between the operators and successive Lebanese governments. \par \par \uc2  Traders said demand for the dollar remained low, and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Banque du Liban, was buying dollars. \par \par \uc2  They said they expected the pound to stay at current levels for the rest of the summer without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Overnight interbank rates were also steady at around eight percent. \par \par \uc2  Lebanon's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tapped its reserves to prop up the pound over the past two years as fears mounted about Lebanon's ability to service its public debt, expected to reach 178 percent of GDP this year. \par \par \uc2  In the short term, the government hopes a conference of potential donors that France has offered to host can provide relief in the form of long-term low-interest loans. Dealers said optimism over that conference was also helping the pound. \par \par \uc2  Pressure on the pound fell in May after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold some $950 million of a sovereign Eurobond holding, helping replenish foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said gross \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were $4.49 billion at end-July, down from about $7.6 billion in early 2000. The bank does not reveal net hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which most analysts believe are significantly lower. \par \par \uc2  ($1=1,507.5 Lebanese pounds). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020809dy8900kzw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
