\par\par \b \uc2  Cellphone truce keeps Lebanon pound stable. \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2002\par 16:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, May 17 (Reuters) - The Lebanese pound was stable in the week ending Friday, as traders said a truce in a government row over a telecoms privatisation that is a key to plans for handling crippling public debt reassured the market. \par \par \uc2  However, they said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained the only supplier of dollars on the market as overnight interest rates fluctuated at a relatively high 11-15 percent. Overnight rates usually hover around seven or eight percent. \par \par \uc2  The Lebanese pound changed hands at 1,514 to the dollar, the upper limit of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 1,501-1,514 pounds to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has mounted in recent weeks during a row between the president and prime minister over a planned sale of two cellular phone licences the government hopes will raise revenue to help handle its $27 billion public debt, which is expected to reach 178 percent of GDP by yearend. \par \par \uc2  The feuding leaders agreed this week on a broad plan to either auction those licences or rights to operate their networks by the end of August. \par \par \uc2  "The market calmed a bit once a deal was reached," said one dealer, adding that any relief for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would ultimately depend on pushing ahead with those sales. \par \par \uc2  "Only progress in privatisation can really ease the pressure," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as public finances sour, seeing its gross \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves drop from the equivalent of $7.6 billion at the end of 2000 to $4.6 billion by mid-April. It does not disclose net hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which are thought to be much lower. \par \par \uc2  The bank raised deposit reserve requirements last year in a bid to give itself more space to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and last month hiked interest rates on two-year t-bills to 16.14 percent from 14.14 percent in an attempt to lure people to the pound. ($1=1,507.5 Lebanese pounds). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020517dy5h00t0y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
