\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanon pound stable, cenbank on sidelines. \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2002\par 15:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Jan 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to maintain a stable exchange rate this week after demand rose for the Lebanese pound , dealers said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  They said the interbank exchange rate remained unchanged at 1,514 pounds to the dollar and the Banque du Liban stopped offering a 16 percent yield on Lebanese pound bonds instead of 14 percent to create demand for the pound. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said even without the premium offered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the bills, the spread on pound holdings compared to dollars was high enough to create demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars, it was in very small quantities," said a dealer at a large bank. \par \par \uc2  Wadih Sabbagh, chief dealer at Byblos Bank, said the pound had started 2002 on a better note. \par \par \uc2  "We have clients who switched significant deposits to the pound. But they are freezing them for short periods - three months at most," Sabbagh added. \par \par \uc2  He expected pressure on the pound to resume if the government did not secure international assistance to control the public debt and did not work hard to streamline and sell loss-making state enterprises. \par \par \uc2  A public debt that exceeded 160 percent of gross domestic product last year has lessened confidence in the pound and forced the monetary authorities to defend it, by buying treasury bills and offering premiums to those already in the market. \par \par \uc2  The bank also has sold dollars from its reserves, which fell 20 percent to $4.72 billion at the end of 2001. \par \par \uc2  In a research note Banque Audi said that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings of Lebanese pound treasury bills had risen to 6,000 billion (about $4 billion) by the end of 2001. ($1=1,508 Lebanese pounds). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020111dy1b00rmu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
