\par\par \b \uc2  Calm returns to Lebanese pound after U.S. row. \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2001\par 17:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Nov 16 (Reuters) - The Lebanese pound was steady this week as calm returned to the market following a recent political dispute with the United States over money laundering, dealers said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  They said the exchange rate was stable at near the upper end of Banque du Liban's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 1,514 pounds to the dollar with supply of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  coming from within the market. \par \par \uc2  "The spreads are in the pound's favour. They are overshadowing the disagreement with Washington and encouraging depositors to switch to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Nabil Chaya, head of treasury at Banque Audi, said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly in the market last week after \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  refused a U.S. demand to seize the assets of the Hizbollah guerrilla group. Washington said it would consider taking retaliatory action against Lebanese banks. \par \par \uc2  The banks do a large proportion of their business in or through the United States. Their health is crucial to the governments strategy of defending the pound. \par \par \uc2  The banks buy most of Lebanon's $26 billion public debt and contribute significantly to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased demand for the pound with swap \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  that raised the yield on the benchmark two-year treasury bill to 16 percent compared to the two percent federal funds rate. \par \par \uc2  Financiers said monetary authorities were buying time and that the government had to make reforms and succeed in receiving international support to control the debt. \par \par \uc2  Wadih Sabbagh, chief dealer at Byblos Bank, expected investors to switch to the pound as Lebanese banks start cutting interest rates on dollar deposits from 5-6 percent to 4.5-5.5 percent in response to the U.S. cuts. \par \par \uc2  "The interest rates differential is the main factor driving the market at present," said Sabbagh. \par \par \uc2  ($1=1,507.5 Lebanese pounds). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011116dxbg00uq0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
