\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Lebanon reserves fall to $4.146 bln at end August. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sultan Sleiman \par \uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2001\par 12:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Sept 3 (Reuters) - Lebanon's gross foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to 6.251 trillion Lebanese pounds ($4.146 billion) at the end of August from 6.838 trillion pounds in mid-August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Reserves stood at about $4.77 billion at the end of July compared with about $5.9 billion at the end of 2000 and $7.6 billion at the end of 1999. The reserve figure includes deposits by commercial banks and state agencies. \par \par \uc2  Bankers attributed the fall to a political storm that swept the country when the army arrested 200 members of Christian opposition groups in a crackdown against those opposed to Syrian influence in Lebanon. \par \par \uc2  The arrests sparked a feud between pro-Syrian President Emile Lahoud and Prime Minister Rafik al-Hariri who said his government had not been informed about the move. Politicians warned that cabinet had been handcuffed and that Lebanon was in danger of becoming a dictatorship run by Syria. \par \par \uc2  "Lebanon lost millions of dollars because of the differences between officials while the country needs every dollar to face the huge public debt," a banker told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Political tensions have taken their toll on the Lebanese pound on whose behalf the bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to support. \par \par \uc2  They have also compounded anxiety about \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 25 billion public debt, which exceeds 155 percent of GDP, huge budget deficit and doubts about whether the government can deal with the problem at a time of zero economic growth. \par \par \uc2  "The big fall of reserves is a warning to Lebanese officials to put their differences aside and deal with the political and economic problems facing their country," the banking source, who requested anonymity, added. \par \par \uc2  Both Lahoud and Hariri mended fences at the end of last month after the army released most detainees but investors' confidence has yet to be restored. \par \par \uc2  Syria has some 20,000 troops and hundreds of thousands of workers in Lebanon. Their presence rankles with many Lebanese, particularly Christians, who resent Syria's domination of Lebanese politics. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which traders say is generally the only seller of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  locally, does not disclose net reserve levels. \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 1,507.5 Lebanese pounds since September 1999). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010903dx9300k2y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
