\par\par \b \uc2  Politics compounds pressure on Lebanon pound. \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2001\par 14:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Aug 17 (Reuters) - Pressure mounted on Lebanon's ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week as political tension added to anxiety over the country's massive debt and weak finances, traders said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  They said the pound traded at the top of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 1,501-1,514 to the dollar, as a feud between the cabinet and Lebanon's pro-Syrian president over a crackdown on dissidents opposed to Syria's political domination of the country boosted dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  "There was heavy dollar demand due to what happened, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the only provider of dollars," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a major Lebanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Lebanese security forces last week rounded up about 200 Christian dissidents who want Syria to withdraw its 20,000 troops from Lebanon. \par \par \uc2  The cabinet said it had not been informed of the crackdown beforehand, leading opposition politicians to warn that government had been handcuffed and that the country is in danger of becoming a military dictatorship run by Syria. \par \par \uc2  The political tensions have compounded anxiety about Lebanon's $24 billion public debt, which exceeds 155 percent of GDP, huge budget deficit, and doubts whether the government can handle either problem while the country experiences virtually zero economic growth. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to maintain the exchange rate for months, this week said its gross foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were $4.5 billion, compared to about $5.9 billion at the end of 2000. \par \par \uc2  The bank has also reported falling subscriptions in each of the last several t-bill auctions. This week said it sold no certificates of deposit. \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund warned last month that local banks, long the main consumers of government debt, are recording slower deposit growth and may not be able to meet the government's financing needs. \par \par \uc2  Lebanon's government hopes to whittle down the public debt through a combination of politically sensitive spending cuts and sales of unwieldy state assets. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010817dx8h00ouo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
