\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanon foreign reserves down $14.9 mln in mid-Apr. \b0\par\par\uc2 149 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2000\par 17:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, April 18 (Reuters) - Lebanon's gross foreign reserves fell $14.99 million to $7.253 billion in mid-April from $7.268 billion at the end of March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Gross foreign reserves, which include deposits by commercial banks and government agencies, were $7.352 billion in mid-March. \par \par \uc2  Bankers last week said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in almost a year, selling dollars to shore up the pound. \par \par \uc2  Lebanon ended 1999 with gross reserves of $7.61 billion compared to $6.41 billion in 1998 and $5.93 billion in 1997. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not disclose net reserves. \par \par \uc2  $1 = 1,507.5 Lebanese pounds. \par \par \uc2  ((Beirut newsroom + 9611 983 885/6 fax 983 889 \par \par \uc2  beirut.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4i01wgk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
