\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanon cen.bank supports pound in dull market. \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 1999\par 14:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, April 30 (Reuters) - Lebanon's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars this week to meet thin demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a stagnant but tight \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market was stable this week. There was light demand for dollars but there was no supply so the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $6 million to $7 million," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said light demand kept the interbank dealing range at 1,512.50-1,513.50 pounds to the dollar, which is on the upper range of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the band steady at between 1,502 and 1,514 pounds to the dollar since mid-October when army commander Emile Lahoud was elected president. \par \par \uc2  Violence in the south, where Israel occupies a 15 km (nine mile) wide zone, and economic indicators had put a damper on the market, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Investors see the tense situation in the south on one hand and the government's decision to start collecting donations and its budget on the other hand and they've decided to halt their investments," he said. \par \par \uc2  This week, seven Israeli soldiers, three pro-Israeli South Lebanon Army militiamen and three civilians were wounded in south Lebanon fighting. \par \par \uc2  The government on Wednesday decided to establish a fund for Lebanese emigrants to collect contributions while a parliamentary committee started discussing the 1999 budget bill, which targets a deficit of 40.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Who will be encouraged to invest in a country that is collecting donations?" another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supplied the market with $20 million a week ago and with $50 million a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  ((Beirut newsroom +9611 745 306/8 fax 745 336 \par \par \uc2  beirut.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4u01uud\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
