\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  sells dollars to support pound. \b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 1999\par 11:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, April 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to meet light demand for the U.S. dollar in the week ended on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market was very calm this week. There was light demand for dollars but there was no supply so the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold about $20 million," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said after Israel annexed the village of Arnoun to its south Lebanon occupation zone last week investors feared further Israeli military actions ahead of parliamentary elections in the Jewish state scheduled for May 17. \par \par \uc2  The previous week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  supplied the market with $50 million. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said light demand for dollars kept interbank dealing on the upper edge of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, which has been steady at 1,502-1,514 pounds to the dollar since mid-October when army commander Emile Lahoud was elected president. \par \par \uc2  ((Beirut newsroom +9611 745 306/8 fax 745 336 \par \par \uc2  beirut.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4n02gqm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
