\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr demand wanes in Beirut, investors await budget. \b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 11:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, March 19 (Reuters) - Pressure on the Lebanese pound continued to ease this week in a lifeless foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market which dealers said was awaiting the 1999 budget. \par \par \uc2  They said the pound "comfortably" traded within the official band set by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 , making \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market unnecessary. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been largely supplying the market with dollars since December to prevent the pound from moving outside a range that has stood at between 1,502 pounds and 1,514 pounds to the dollar so far this year. \par \par \uc2  One dealer, who put the total size of the market at $50 to $60 million, said the lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not be interpreted much as a very positive sign. \par \par \uc2  "The market is completely frozen. The mood is lingering ahead of the budget," he said. \par \par \uc2  Investors have been waiting to see the 1999 budget and the government's efforts to reduce a deficit that finished at around 14 percent of GDP last year. The budget was due by the beginning of March but has been delayed. \par \par \uc2  ((Beirut editorial (9611) 745 308 fax 745336 \par \par \uc2  beirut.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv3j0230l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
