\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Central bank \highlight\uc2  helps Lebanese pound in quiet market. \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 1998\par 12:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Sept 11 (Reuters) - The Lebanese pound made gains with the help of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a quiet market in the week ended on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band stood in the range of 1,504.50-1,517.50 compared with 1,505.00-1,518.00 last Friday. \par \par \uc2  "There was some commercial demand for U.S. dollars with little supply but the market was quiet," said a dealer who requested anonymity. \par \par \uc2  "This week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold between $35 million and $40 million to support the pound," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was due to market anxiety over presidential elections due to be held next month. \par \par \uc2  "Some investors prefer to wait until the presidential elections are over before they involve themselves in any new Lebanese pound-denominated treasury bills," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Lebanon is planning to have presidential elections in October. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said he expected Lebanon's successful placement of $350 million of new debt on international markets on Thursday to boost confidence in the country, \par \par \uc2  "The placement of the bond issue took place on Thursday. So we have to wait for next week to see its results. But I think this issue represents a renewal of the international community's confidence in Lebanon," he said. \par \par \uc2  Interbank trading stood at 1,517.50-1,518.00 against last week's 1,517.75-1,518.25, he added. \par \par \uc2  ((Beirut editorial (9611) 745308 fax 745336 \par \par \uc2  beirut.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9b00wqd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
