\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound faces pressure, then recovers. \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 12:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, July 31 (Reuters) - The Lebanese pound faced a bout of mid-week pressure because of increased political tension, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band stood at 1,508.00-1,520.00 Lebanese pounds for a dollar compared to last week's 1,508.50-1,520.50 - the rate of appreciation set by the government in the past couple of years. \par \par \uc2  "The market was quiet at the beginning of the week. But under the impact of the political confusion we witnessed some artificial demand (for dollars) on Wednesday and Thursday," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "On Friday, supply of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was much more than demand and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $8.0 million. The total volume of the market this week was about $50 million," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Interbank trading was 1,508.00-1,508.15 for a dollar against last week's range of 1,508.25-1,508.50, he said. \par \par \uc2  The powerful Parliament Speaker Nabih Berri and Prime Minister Rafik al-Hariri this week accused each other of violating the constitution. It reflected tension in advance of a presidential election expected in October. \par \par \uc2  (Beirut editorial (9611) 745-308 fax 745336 \par \par \uc2  beirut.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du7v013fe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
