\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound boosted by dollar selling. \b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 1998\par 13:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, May 29 (Reuters) - Lebanon's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars this week amid upward pressure on the Lebanese pound from a rush into local treasury bills, dealers said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band stood at 1,512.50-1,524.50 Lebanese pounds to the dollar compared to last week's range of 1,513-1,525, continuing the steady appreciation of the official rate. \par \par \uc2  But a dealer said the rise this week reflected funadamentals in the market, with investors rushing to buy Lebanese treasury bills and lock in high annual interest rates that have begun to decline. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying dollars on an average of $15 million to $20 million a day in the last two weeks," said another dealer. \par \par \uc2  "We saw a little demand for the dollar from two banks only, probably for some private \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But this did not influence the trend of supply of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Interbank trading was in the range of 1,512.60-1,512.75 pounds to the dollar against last week's 1,513-1,513.25, he added. \par \par \uc2  ((Beirut editorial (9611) 745308 fax 745336 \par \par \uc2  beirut.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5t047oz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
