\par\par \b \uc2  UAE deposit boosts Lebanese pound in week. \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, May 8 (Reuters) - The Lebanese pound continued to gain against the U.S. dollar on the three working days of the week ended on Friday, with dealers reporting that a $100 million United Arab Emirates deposit in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosted the pound. \par \par \uc2  Lebanon's financial markets were closed on Wednesday and Thursday for holidays. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band stood at 1,514-1,526 pounds to the dollar on Friday from last Friday's 1,514-1,526.50. \par \par \uc2  Interbank trading was at the lower edge of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band and reached 1,514-1,514.50 Lebanese pounds to the dollar on Friday from last week's 1,515.50-1,516.50, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "There was quite a good amount of supply of dollars in the market and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a buyer for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the pound was boosted by the restored confidence in Lebanon caused by the $100 million UAE deposit in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the $1 billion bond issue in March. \par \par \uc2  "There was a supply of dollar this week following reports about the $100 million UAE deposit in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The UAE deposit and the previous Saudi and Kuwaiti deposits and the $1 billion Eurobond issue encouraged foreign investors to return to the treasury bills market," he added. \par \par \uc2  On Monday Lebanon said it had reached an agreement with UAE for a $100 million deposit for three years starting May 7. \par \par \uc2  In January, Kuwait deposited $100 million with Lebanon's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at five percent interest rate for three years. This followed a Saudi Arabian deposit of $500 million at the same interest rate for three years and $100 million to be spent on investment infrastructure. \par \par \uc2  In March, Lebanon raised $1.0 billion on the international market via two well-received bond issues with five-and three-year maturities. \par \par \uc2  ((Beirut newsroom (9611) 745308 fax 745336 \par \par \uc2  beirut.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5805sos\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
