\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound gains by end of week on budget hopes. \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Oct 17 (Reuters) - The Lebanese pound gained ground by the close of the week ending on Friday after political leaders put aside their differences over the 1998 budget, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said demand for the dollar had eased at the end of the week after Prime Minister Rafik al-Hariri and Parliament Speaker Nabih Berri ended a dispute over the budget, which still needs parliamentary approval. \par \par \uc2  "At the end of the week the market was much better after the two leaders came to an agreement," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Lebanese pound has been more sensitive to events in the political arena since Hariri's plan to partly finance a controversial $800 million development plan by raising petrol prices was rejected by the cabinet on September 24. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Lebanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had recovered from the cabinet's decision last week. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was 1527.00-1537.00 Lebanese pounds compared to last week's 1527.50-1537.50. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  but not that much because demand for the dollar decreased by the end of the week," said another dealer. \par \par \uc2  Inter-bank dollar trading was in the range of 1536.00-1538.50 against last week's 1537.00-1538.50. \par \par \uc2  - Beirut editorial (9611) 745308 745307 602057 \par \par \uc2  beirut.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtah048ef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580