\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Lebanon  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves fall in mid-Sept. \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Sept 17 (Reuter) - The Bank of Lebanon's gross \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell in the first half of September for the first time in 17 months, dropping $160.44 million to $6.437 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Banking sources said the drop in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves was mainly because commercial banks withdrew a total of $110.44 million from deposits at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  This was the first drop in the gross foreign reserves of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the second half of April 1996 when they dropped by $95.67 million to $4.683 billion. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Riad Salameh said the bank would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, keeping a narrow bid-offer spread and ensuring a steady appreciation of the Lebanese pound which collapsed during the 1975-90 civil war. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered its bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 1529.50-1539.50 pounds to the dollar against 1530.00-1540.00 a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  Gross reserves had risen by $1.5 million in the second half of August to $6.598 billion. They include commercial banks' net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The bank gave no figure for net reserves but banking sources said they dropped to $4.350 billion in mid-September from $4.400 billion at the end of August. \par \par \uc2  According to the banking sources, net reserves stood at $4.015 billion at the end of 1996 compared with $2.858 a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  - Beirut editorial (961 1) 745307 745308 602057 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9h02d0j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
