\par\par \b \uc2  B.of  \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon intervened \highlight\uc2  in past wk on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, July 11 (Reuter) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Beirut \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to meet demand for dollars in the week ended on Friday, selling the dollars for 1,543 Lebanese pounds, at the top of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1,543 from Monday to Thursday but stopped on Friday when dollar supply reappeared on the market and the pound climbed to 1,542-1,542.75 in interbank trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It was the second week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the top of its bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to sell dollars. It sold at 1,543-1,543.5 last week. \par \par \uc2  The bank changed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band during the past week to 1,534.5-1,543 from 1,535.5-1,543. \par \par \uc2  "Yesterday and every day before that we were buying dollars at the Bank of Lebanon rate of 1,543 pounds, but today there was a bit of dollar supply on the market so we were dealing below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate at 1,542-1,542.75," a dealer who asked not to be identified told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "At the end of the week there were some good signs because I think there is some saturation on the market and there is a supply of dollars," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers last week said political problems were causing increased demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  They cited a civil disobedience campaign launched in eastern Lebanon by a radical Shi'ite cleric, a dispute between President Elias Hrawi and Prime Minister Rafik al-Hariri over command of internal security troops and a flare-up of fighting in south Lebanon between Moslem guerrillas and Israeli troops. \par \par \uc2  -Beirut editorial (9611) 345723 345740 602057 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7b02r7v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
