\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanon pound falls on political ills-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, July 4 (Reuter) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Beirut \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the week ended on Friday, selling dollars at the upper limit of its bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to meet demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the Lebanese pound fell to 1,543.5 to the dollar on Thursday and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday to buy pounds at 1,543 -- the upper limit of the band. Dealers cited political uncertainties for the trend. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band during the week to 1,535.5-1,543 pounds per dollar from last week's 1,535.5-1,544. \par \par \uc2  The pound traded in inter-bank trade last week in a range of 1,539-1,542.5. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was a small amount of inter-bank trade at prices 25 to 50 piastres below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate but most of the demand for dollars could not be met by commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sold dollars in the market. Many banks bought from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer who asked not to be identified said of this week's trade. \par \par \uc2  "Last week there was a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling price for dollars but the market was below this. This week the market reached the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate and banks bought dollars from it," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Many banks bought dollars directly from the Bank of Lebanon because there was some demand for dollars and no supply because of the political situation," he added. \par \par \uc2  He cited a civil disobedience campaign launched in eastern Lebanon on Friday by a radical Shi'ite cleric, a dispute between President Elias Hrawi and Prime Minister Rafic al-Hariri over command of internal security troops and fighting in south Lebanon between Moslem guerrillas and Israeli troops. \par \par \uc2  "Because of all this there was some tension in the market and demand for dollars," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7403357\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
