\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound edges down on week. \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, June 27 (Reuter) - The Lebanese pound edged closer to the upper end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in the week ended on Friday amid continued demand for U.S. dollars on the Beirut \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar traded in inter-bank trade in a range of 1,539-1,542.5 pounds compared with 1,538-1,541 last week and 1,536-1,537.5 the week before, they said. \par \par \uc2  This was near the upper end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band which the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered during the week to 1,535.5-1,544 pounds per dollar from last week's 1,535.5-1,545. \par \par \uc2  "I think the highest deal during the week was 1,542.5, but 1,543 was the highest price quoted," a dealer who asked not to be identified told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  He said there was some supply of dollars and the market was balanced. \par \par \uc2  "We didn't reach (top end of) the Bank of Lebanon rate. I don't think anyone bought dollars from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said last week restrictions of allocations of shorter-term pound-denominated treasury bills by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were helping to boost demand for dollars as investors who were allowed to buy only a small fraction of the bills they bid for changed their excess funds back to dollars. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, dealers said there was no change of trend on the market on which the Lebanese pound has steadily appreciated against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the past five years. \par \par \uc2  However, the dollar was routinely in over-supply for several months until early June and traded for weeks in a tight range of a few dozen piastres at the bottom of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2  Asked why the dollar was now more in demand, a dealer said restrictions on t-bill allocations were still affecting the market and there was some political tension. \par \par \uc2  This appeared a reference to controversy over the government's June 10 decision to raise import duties on cars and ban imports of some food products from October in a bid to reduce the heavy trade deficit and stimulate local agriculture. \par \par \uc2  -Beirut editorial (9611) 345723 345740 602057 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6r03a8m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
