\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound firms against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, April 14 (Reuter) - The Lebanese pound regained ground against the U.S. dollar in quiet interbank trade in Beirut on Monday and dealers said the market was calming down after a flurry of activity last week. \par \par \uc2  The market opened at 1,546-1,549 pounds to the dollar from 1,548.5 on Friday, but the Lebanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed steadily during the morning to 1,543-1,545, a dealer who asked not to be identified told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The pound moved at the close to 1,545-1,548 per dollar as some banks closed their positions, the dealer added. He estimated trade at $4-$5 million. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was unchanged from last week's 1,540-1549.5 pounds per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "All trade was within the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate and there was some selling of dollars by banks due to treasury bill purchases and the Eid al-Adha holiday on Thursday," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  "I think it is a matter of time before we have a calm market again. There was nothing special today," he said. \par \par \uc2  Last week the pound fell six points against the dollar within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in interbank trade as one commercial bank bought a large amount of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , putting pressure on the Lebanese pound. \par \par \uc2  - Beirut editorial (961 1) 345723 345740 602057 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt