\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound eases against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, April 11 (Reuter) - The Lebanese pound fell back against the dollar in interbank trade in the week ended on Friday amid heavy demand for U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said commercial banks traded the pound at 1548.5 per dollar -- six pounds stronger than the previous week's interbank rate of 1,542.5 and 2.5 pounds above Thursday's 1,546. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered its bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band during the week to 1,540-1549.5 pounds per dollar from 1,540.5-1,550 last week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a large dollar order by one commercial bank created pressure at the beginning of the week. \par \par \uc2  "Demand for dollars continued as a result of political uncertainty arising from the issue of municipal elections," Nabil Abou Jaoude, Treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager for Banque Libanaise pour le Commerce told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The government's withdrawal of the elections bill last week angered President Elias Hrawi, Christian and leftist opposition and caused concern that the government might delay the elections which are due in June. \par \par \uc2  "Another factor is the restrictions imposed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on short term treasury bills which led non-resident investors to shift to U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Pressure on the market slowed down trading \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Despite many questions asked on the market, trade was thin today. It seems everyone was in a wait-and-see state after the bid-offer margin was close to one pound," Abou Jaoude said. \par \par \uc2  All demand for dollars was met by commercial banks without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Shadi Hanna Treasurer for Bank Byblos told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "The market was very normal and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in full control. The rise of the U.S. dollar is a technical matter," Hanna said. \par \par \uc2  -Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4b07635\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
