\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound wobbles on political uncertainty. \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, April 4 (Reuter) - The Lebanese pound initially continued its steady rise against the U.S. dollar for the first three days of the week but fell back slightly in interbank trade on Friday due to political uncertainties, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered its bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band during the week to 1,540.5-1550 pounds per dollar from 1,541-1,550.5. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said commercial banks traded the pound from Tuesday to Thursday after the long Easter weekend at 1,541.5 per dollar -- one pound stronger than the previous week's interbank rate of 1,542.5. \par \par \uc2  However, Thursday's resignation of Constitutional Council chief Wajdi al-Mallat and the government's withdrawal of a bill to amend the municipal elections law sparked increased dollar demand on Friday and the pound fell back to 1,542.5 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  All demand for dollars was met by commercial banks without \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The withdrawal of the elections bill caused concern among politicians and the media that the government might delay the first local elections since 1963 which are due in June. \par \par \uc2  "Trade among banks was quiet in the first three days of the week at one pound above the bid end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band," Talal Abou Zaki, \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Manager for Bank Beirut and the Arab Countries said, "but due to political confusion on Thursday the dollar was traded two pounds above the bid end." \par \par \uc2  "The resignation of the head of Constitutional Council and indications of a postponement of municipal elections had some effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade in the market," Abou Zaki said. \par \par \uc2  Mallat resigned amid reports that the Constitutional Council was facing heavy political pressures over appeals it is handling against the results of last year's parliamentary elections. \par \par \uc2  The withdrawal of the elections bill raised expectations of a possible dispute between Prime Minister Rafik al-Hariri and President Elias Hrawi who has made clear that he opposes any delay in holding the elections. \par \par \uc2  -Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4407qod\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
