\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound continues rise against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, March 14 (Reuter) - The Lebanese pound continued rising against the U.S. dollar in the week ended on Friday, and dealers said the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision to exempt banks from mandatory t-bill subscriptions relaxed the market. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered its bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to 1,542-1,551.5 pounds per dollar from last week's 1,542-1,552.5, and the dollar traded at the bottom of the band throughout the week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Nabil Abou Jaoude, Treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Manager at Banque Libanaise pour Le Commerce, said trade was restricted to a tight range of up to 65 piastres at the bid end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  There was some demand for dollars, but all was met by the banks, he said. \par \par \uc2  Market sentiment was positively affected by Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision to exempt commercial banks from compulsory subscription of 40 percent of their Lebanese pound deposits in treasury bills, Abou Jaoude said. \par \par \uc2  "This decision left a positive psychological influence on the market, and we still await for more relaxing decisions from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  -Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt3e08nxm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
