\par\par \b \uc2  Exotic  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Focus: Lebanon Pays For Strong Pound \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shanthy Nambiar \par \uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 1997\par 22:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  New York (AP-Dow Jones)--High hopes are being pinned on a comprehensive Middle East peace settlement and Lebanon's multi-billion dollar reconstruction program to ensure the continued stability of the Lebanese pound. \par \par \uc2  With the combined economic benefits of a peace agreement and a restored infrastructure, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be able to abandon its policy of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and high interest rates that it has used to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some analysts said. \par \par \uc2  This in turn could relieve the country's yawning fiscal deficit, a result of spending for reconstruction programs and debt servicing, which some analysts warn is inflationary and could subvert the government's efforts to maintain a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Suha Najjar, a Middle East analyst at Nomura Research in London, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't expected to relax its monetary policy until the country enjoys greater political and economic stability. \par \par \uc2  The pound has appreciated 18% against the U.S. dollar since the beginning of 1993 and was quoted at a dollar rate of 1550 Tuesday by Banque Saradar S.A.L. in Lebanon. \par \par \uc2  In 1992, as Lebanon was beginning its recovery from a 16-year civil war that left damages estimated at $30 billion, the pound was at a dollar rate of 2,000. \par \par \uc2  Since then, the government of Prime Minister Rafik al-Hariri has maintained a steadfast policy of strengthening the pound as a means to restoring investor confidence in the post-war economy. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-01-97 \par \par \uc2  2100GMT \par \par \uc2  1106 1838 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1s00gdx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
