\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound strengthens further during week. \b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Jan 17 (Reuter) - The Lebanese pound continued its steady appreciation against the U.S. dollar in the week ended Friday on a quiet market with a continued oversupply of dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered its bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to 1,546-1,555.50 pounds per dollar from 1,546.5-1,556 and the dollar again traded at the bottom of the band throughout the week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought most of the dollars on offer and commercial banks absorbed only 15-20 percent, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "People are not buying dollars and the amounts offered are above the banks' commercial requirements," Talal Abou Zaki, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager for Bank of Beirut and the Arab Countries, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Trade was limited to a very tight band of 10-25 piastres at the bid end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, Abou Zaki said. \par \par \uc2  After the Bank lowered its bid rate to 1,546 pounds on Tuesday, the dollar traded at 1,546-1,546.25 or 1,546.05-1,546.15, he added. \par \par \uc2  "The mood is still in favour of the Lebanese pound because people are convinced by the high interest rates on the pound and have no fears about the political or security situation," Abou Zaki said. \par \par \uc2  -Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 345740 345723 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt1h051ls\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal6