\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese pound strengthens in quiet market. \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Nov 29 (Reuter) - The Lebanese pound strengthened against the dollar in the week ended on Friday with trade confined to a tight 15-25 piastres spread at the bottom of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market was not very active, they said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice adjusted its bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band by 50 piastres during the week to reach 1,550-1,558 Lebanese pounds per dollar from 1,551-1,558 at last Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  Political events, including a sometimes hard-hitting parliamentary confidence debate on Prime Minister Rafik al-Hariri's new government followed by a partially effective general strike on Thursday against Hariri's policies, had no impact on the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The political events did not affect the market in the least," a dealer with a Beirut bank told Reuters. "The market was very calm." \par \par \uc2  Most banks ignored Thursday's strike and financial markets including \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers stayed open during the stoppage. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said the pound traded throughout the week at 1,550.05-1,550.20 per dollar and another said the range was 1,550.0-1,550.25. \par \par \uc2  "There was good offer of dollars. People were buying Lebanese pounds. It is all because of the expectation of falling interest rates on Lebanese pound treasury bills," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  -Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 353078 861723 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dsbt02ud7\pa