\par\par \b \uc2  Beirut  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market quiet during week. \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Nov 15 (Reuter) - Beirut's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was quiet during the week ending on Friday, with trading mostly confined to a very narrow spread at the lower end of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened its bid-offer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to 1,551-1,559 Lebanese pounds per dollar from 1,552-1,559 on the previous Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Interbank trade was very light during the week. Nothing to mention," Wadih Sabbagh, chief dealer at Byblos Bank said. \par \par \uc2  This was due to the market quieting down after the installation of Prime Minister Rafik al-Hariri's new government and to the economic situation, he said. \par \par \uc2  "As there is no speculation, the market was left to commercial transactions. And most merchants say they have no deals because there are no commercial transactions," Sabbagh added. \par \par \uc2  Talal Abou Zaki, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Bank of Beirut and the Arab Countries, said there was slight dollar demand on Monday, but banks offered dollars for the rest of the week. \par \par \uc2  The market traded at 1,552.5-1,553.5 on Monday, but the spread narrowed by the end of the week to 25 piastres or even 15 piastres, Abou Zaki said. \par \par \uc2  "Today, I gave quotes to some banks for 1,551.10-1,551.25," he said. \par \par \uc2  He believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday and Thursday to buy dollars at 1,551.50. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there is going to be much change in the market or in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in the near future because we have got over the worst -- the change of government and all that," Abou Zaki said. \par \par \uc2  Andrew Tarnowski-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 353078 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018dsbf00e9b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
