\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon \highlight\uc2  changes  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  method. \b0\par\par\uc2 455 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Sept 26 (Reuter) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  has changed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanism on the Beirut \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by shifting from a single mid-price quotation to a bid-offer system, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank has since Tuesday set a difference of three Lebanese pounds between the prices at which it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy and sell dollars, the dealers said. \par \par \uc2  This replaces a single mid-price at which it either bought or sold dollars in the past, depending on the market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the change would stimulate interbank trading, making the market less dependent on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and more on supply and demand. \par \par \uc2  "This gives us dealers the opportunity to quote between each other. I believe it's very good," Wadih Sabbagh, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Byblos Bank, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered on Thursday to buy dollars at 1,557 pounds and to sell at 1,560. The dollar closed at 1,558.75. \par \par \uc2  Sabbagh said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Club-Liban had asked \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Riad Salameh nine months ago to set buying and selling prices to allow a spread for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers to quote, and the World Bank had recommended the change. \par \par \uc2  "We expected this earlier, but now they have responded," Sabbagh said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's practice of setting a single price for the past few years had idled Beirut dealers by making the market dependent on the Bank of Lebanon for buying and selling dollars, he said. \par \par \uc2  Another Beirut dealer who asked not to be identified said the Bank of Lebanon had set the band very narrow to maintain stability while giving leeway for commercial banks to make a market within those boundaries. \par \par \uc2  "It's not very significant because they are setting the boundaries in a very narrow band," the dealer said, "but in the longer term I think it's a step in the right direction because it will make the market more affected by supply and demand rather than just by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was taking advantage of a surge of confidence in the pound on the Beirut market during the past four weeks. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's a very clear sign of confidence in the pound," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said investors were selling dollars to buy pounds, but if tension developed in the system the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would narrow the band. \par \par \uc2  "But I think with time, if we remain in a stable scenario, the band will tend to widen....Bit by bit we are moving more towards supply and demand in the interbank market." \par \par \uc2  -- Andrew Tarnowski - Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 353078 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds9q02j1f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
