\par\par \b \uc2  Lebanese buy dollars as Israeli blitz continues. \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 1996\par 13:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, April 16 (Reuter) - Lebanon's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  faced demand for dollars on Tuesday because of Israel's six-day blitz on the country, but the Lebanese pound held steady at 1,581.5 to the dollar with the help of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "In \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the political situation always manifests itself on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," a banker told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers who asked not to be identified estimated that the Bank of Lebanon sold between $50 million and $70 million to institutions and individuals exchanging Lebanese pounds. \par \par \uc2  This contrasted with the more usual pattern in recent weeks of the Bank buying up to $10 million a day to meet demand for Lebanese pounds from customers investing in high-yielding Lebanese treasury bills. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's rate of 1,581.5 Lebanese pounds to the dollar was unchanged from last Thursday when the Israeli blitz began and the market closed for the four-day Greek Orthodox Easter weekend. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves currently stand at a record level of about $3 billion and a banking source said it was able to meet the demand "pretty easily." \par \par \uc2  "But the scope, length and term of the crisis, nobody can tell," the source said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no panic on the market. "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a very good way, selling and buying at 1,581.5 pounds to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "So the exchange rate is not being affected because the Bank can control it," a dealer told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The Lebanese pound has appreciated steadily against the dollar since billionaire construction tycoon Rafik al-Hariri became prime minister in October 1992, vowing to rebuild the country from the 1975-90 civil war. \par \par \uc2  Political crises in the past three-and-a-half years have regularly caused runs on the pound but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has defended it each time and averted any depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  - Andrew Tarnowski, Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 353078 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds4g0993d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
