\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Lebanon to continue defending pound. \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIRUT, Sept 16 (Reuter) - Lebanon's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue its policy of defending the Lebanese pound on the Beirut \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Bank of Lebanon governor Riad Salameh was quoted on Saturday as saying. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank will stay in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the Lebanese pound's exchange rate," as-Safir daily quoted Salameh as saying at a meeting on Friday with officials of Lebanon's Banks Association grouping Beirut's 82 banks. \par \par \uc2  Salameh's remark came a day after a grouping of Lebanese businessmen said in a report that the Bank should stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as soon as possible to allow for a real market to emerge. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Lebanon\b0 \highlight\uc2  often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market selling U.S. dollars to defend the pound, especially in times of political crisis which usually witness a flight from the local to the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The policy of defending the pound depleted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by more than $1 billion between January and June. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the usefulness of such a policy that was depleting the Bank's reserves, Salameh replied: \par \par \uc2  "I am not afraid of more defence of the pound if the 1996 public budget comes out as it should come out, especially as there will be remittances (from abroad) that have begun to flow again". \par \par \uc2  Salameh said there was an agreement with the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  on lowering all items in the 1996 budget draft "so that the deficit would not exceed 40 percent for any reason". \par \par \uc2  He said he was relieved for the disappearance of selling pressure on the pound witnessed recently. The run was caused by a political crisis between Prime Minister Rafik al-Hariri and Parliament Speaker Nabih Berri that was solved last week. \par \par \uc2  In a second step to boost the pound, Salameh said he was in contact with the ministries of finance, and economy and trade, to take measures forcing merchants to use the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in transactions. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr9g03y4b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
